🫦 Togetherly • v1.28.4

— Widgets are back in the iPhone gallery. The extension crashed on launch, so the system could never learn which widgets the app has — and Togetherly was missing from the list entirely.
— One icon on the home screen again: those who had picked a coloured icon ended up with two after an update.
— The "Miss you" counter stops losing taps: a burst tapped out before you close the app now reaches your partner in full.
— The "Days together" widget no longer says "0 years already" — before the first anniversary it counts in months.
— The timer list for widgets shows the symbol itself, not its internal name.
— A partner's comment on a memory now arrives as a notification.
— Settings now link to our channel and to the bot that collects bug reports.
